## How to read this report

- Engines are never averaged together: each has its own section, named by surface, model, tool version and config.
- Activation is how often an answer searched the web. Read, cited, FootnoteOne and conversion count only searched answers to unbranded intents (read, cited and FootnoteOne as one mean per intent); activation counts every answer whose activation is known, whatever the intent, and unconditional cited every such answer to an unbranded intent, searched or not.
- Each value has its 95% interval in parentheses, then what was counted and the method. A Student t interval over intents can run below 0 or above 100 when intents are few; it is shown as computed. "cannot judge" means every intent gave the same value, so the interval has no width. "no data" means nothing was counted, and is never a zero.

